# Compiled C++ drivers & artifacts
cpp/dd_solve
cpp/dd_solve_1d
cpp/dd_solve_2d
cpp/dd_solve*_omp
cpp/dd_solve*_prof
cpp/ma97_smoke
cpp/ma97_smoke_par
cpp/mumps_smoke
*.o
*.dSYM/
*.dwarf

# Solver output (regenerated)
cpp/results/
/results/
cpp/plots/
cpp/sol_*.txt
cpp/dd_*.txt
cpp/*.png

# SLURM logs. The batch scripts write %x_%j.out/.err into SLURM_SUBMIT_DIR, and
# since they now locate the repo themselves that can be the repo root, cpp/ or
# slurm/ — so these are global rather than slurm/-scoped. Nothing tracked has
# either extension; re-check before adding one that should be committed.
*.out
*.err
slurm-*.out

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
# uv: the environment is disposable (.venv above), the lockfile is NOT —
# python/uv.lock is committed so `uv sync` reproduces the exact versions a
# recorded run used.
.uv-cache/

# Rendered figures at the top level / python side
python/*.png
*.png

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
*.swp

# Keep the bundled test images and data despite the *.png / .txt rules above.
# images/ is the package's image directory — everything in it is deliberate, so
# negate the whole thing rather than naming files one at a time (naming them is
# how mariposa.png silently failed to be added the first time).
!images/*.png
!python/images/*.png
!cpp/data/*.txt
